</node>
<node id="&quot;DEFAULTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"AGREEMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Events that constitute a Default following the Closing Date, including breaches of representations, warranties, and payment failures."&lt;SEP&gt;"Section 7 outlines various types of defaults that may occur in a credit agreement, such as Breach of Representations or Warranties, Failure to Make Payments When Due, and Breach of Covenants."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-3f8d309f90236c63cbdbe99963429949cf52b941a2898e25ca92a5c31865b6e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf023d8a063c56705dcb87212bf4c927c8978394473e8991513f7100ef2ad0e7</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-236032ad52b5c77d76ca8b5b9d3ee21fa9d36f49e15211204ee2de8f5df0e70a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GUARANTY ABSOLUTE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"AGREEMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Section 16.03 refers to the absolute guaranty provided in a credit agreement, ensuring that the obligations of the borrower will be met regardless of circumstances."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-50114c97c504fe761ee5bf9ff61f7df5fb6293aa48c05ebc7774d30c0ccc835e</data>
