</node>
<node id="&quot;EURIBOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"BASE RATE BENCHMARK"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A floating interest rate benchmark mentioned in the fallback provisions related to the credit facilities, alongside LIBOR and CDOR."&lt;SEP&gt;"EURIBOR is defined in the definition of 'Eurocurrency Base Rate.'"&lt;SEP&gt;"Euro Interbank Offered Rate, a benchmark rate used in Europe that may be adjusted or replaced as necessary."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Euro Interbank Offered Rate is the rate at which eurozone banks lend money to each other and is an important benchmark for euro-denominated loans."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-e86ff72e75149a1e4989f2e18b97f1c08bc0c56812050e314d6b3d152b159fed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18226adc50d0d43fc9565aeec65a89dd9d347d5730d5e84494f8535da6419cdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c0f0b68eca4939163d14493fb5157bc0af66d4679ed687caf547fea769ae75c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eeec26f077adfdd1561d685690da4017d74add9d0d6ff1b455ea904bd15cd20</data>
