</node>
<node id="&quot;FEDERAL BANKRUPTCY LAWS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"REGULATORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Federal Bankruptcy Laws are the applicable legal statutes that govern bankruptcy proceedings, under which the Borrower or its Major Subsidiaries may seek relief, thereby impacting the terms of the credit agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-dd455f0d03bf315a1eaea1ebddeb91810cd972f43f562e284f3c072128c7039e</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-236032ad52b5c77d76ca8b5b9d3ee21fa9d36f49e15211204ee2de8f5df0e70a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;NEW YORK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"JURISDICTION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The laws governing the loan documents and the obligations of the parties are based on the laws of the state of NEW YORK."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-49b949bd6b938010a265fb14a53b068d725f73af78772772e2b7ee398ddb3783</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-236032ad52b5c77d76ca8b5b9d3ee21fa9d36f49e15211204ee2de8f5df0e70a</data>
