</node>
<node id="&quot;REVOLVING LOAN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FACILITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A loan made by a lender under the provisions outlined in Section 2.01(a) of the agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of credit facility where the Borrower can draw, repay, and redraw loans from the Lender up to the agreed limit."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of credit that allows the borrower to borrow, repay, and borrow again, up to a specified limit as per the terms outlined in the credit agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of loan that allows the Borrower to draw funds repeatedly up to a certain limit and is used here to reimburse the Issuing Lender for amounts drawn from a Letter of Credit."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-aafeb881cd23ba01cc9e7e2ac9636513df83f37fde9301fdf8943aadd66a1a62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2e76bfe06832d96f514332019f438cc910c77413f0617abc31b13b1ced12faa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f9cbbef1c2c0cf8816bda4b8ba3aad31f6b03ee3c5af5eaff09345647127d74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b7175909aee8ce03791965ee234bfe872f940b215b4506ec0f0b1e30d0cf99d</data>
