<node id="&quot;FEDERAL FUNDS RATE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"BASE RATE BENCHMARK"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A fleeting interest rate used as a benchmark to determine other rates, affecting Advances in Dollars."&lt;SEP&gt;"A key interest rate referenced in the credit agreement, determining the cost of borrowing based on transactions with the Federal Reserve System."&lt;SEP&gt;"Federal Funds Rate is the interest rate at which depository institutions lend reserve balances to other depository institutions overnight, relevant for calculations regarding late payments and obligations."&lt;SEP&gt;"The interest rate at which depository institutions lend reserve balances to other depository institutions overnight, serving as a benchmark in the financial industry."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-9d98031430f0b0255f48182995737acdd3844c6fd9557981e0e3bf24bdd46f8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4612e85e877c62baf82cad7c2be4131f22c11ab0ba5b0025b887d602b61f41e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d990607ca6b9c513c4d87a46d457b97a8e231369a24385de07cb159ae613ec7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-788c1a0d88f1541100bf054380b01f260c6ad5ad3928a6c14b72431c8a554338</data>
