</node>
<node id="&quot;EUROCURRENCY LOANS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FACILITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A type of loan offered in a foreign currency, typically at lower interest rates, based on the Eurocurrency Rate."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of loan referencing a currency that is not tied to the borrower's domestic currency, often used for international lending."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eurocurrency Loans are loans that are made in currencies other than the domestic currency of the country in which the lender is located, often involving complex arrangements subject to prior approvals."&lt;SEP&gt;"These are loans under the Advances that utilize the Eurocurrency market for interest rate determination."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-59684afb2e463574cf2aaf600c780e0debe3a298245661d942ad591b5ac883c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-685a00d495c9204f0f1a1fad404c8355f8fbcfe27979b442eb8a80ba6bfa28c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84d7361cb1344ec6b34607e1ffa71f6fa5a0707b1c2af1350dabed4ef3eb78ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4470aa58220853274314c41720613105a1a0ab6fee66f35905d8edd5cb9e8a35</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-236032ad52b5c77d76ca8b5b9d3ee21fa9d36f49e15211204ee2de8f5df0e70a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BENEFICIAL OWNERSHIP REGULATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"REGULATORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A regulation that mandates the Borrower to supply documentation about its ownership structure and individuals."&lt;SEP&gt;"The regulation requires Lenders to obtain, verify, and record information that identifies the Borrower to comply with know-your-customer and anti-money laundering rules."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ecaefa3c2ad5e19bb3010a0abd8a00b9385343a23c01dd136cc52a12bf1c8a23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b623889d303abd944391e0a2b66745bd68fa6a7cc9cbfb87f629bd8c0cc5525</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-236032ad52b5c77d76ca8b5b9d3ee21fa9d36f49e15211204ee2de8f5df0e70a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REGULATORY AUTHORITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"REGULATORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Regulatory authorities are governmental or self-regulatory bodies responsible for overseeing compliance with laws governing credit agreements and financial transactions."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-a8de38d9f190c7d6bcbaaaede79f19cbb59631f72bbfd31261e61e07ea73ad5e</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-236032ad52b5c77d76ca8b5b9d3ee21fa9d36f49e15211204ee2de8f5df0e70a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;PAUL ARENS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"OBLIGOR"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Paul Arens is a Director signing on behalf of the lender in the credit agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-66fd0f9a9180e543fe5145a08d528e6028aba0d4342edd7498580d6806dc63d1</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-236032ad52b5c77d76ca8b5b9d3ee21fa9d36f49e15211204ee2de8f5df0e70a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REVOLVING CREDIT FACILITY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FACILITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A specific type of credit facility provided to the Borrower that allows for the continual borrowing and repayment of funds up to a certain limit."&lt;SEP&gt;"A structured credit facility allowing Borrowers to withdraw, repay, and borrow again, depending on agreements made."&lt;SEP&gt;"The revolving credit facility established pursuant to Article 2, including any increase in such revolving credit facility established pursuant to Section 2.22."&lt;SEP&gt;"The structured credit or loan arrangement that allows the borrower to draw funds, up to a specified limit, during the term of the agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"The type of credit arrangement provided under the agreement to the Borrower for specified purposes."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-64d3d8235da6ab2d73914174a1596810ac479be1cca3c369228533b49ce78efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9647a89a58b5dd94c4107a499b784dee152c76826fe46e047c882f3d29f4565&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c949aa98795a964a83fee0d2a5cf1003c8a3dcd6bd2a627dc984864d17e0a5d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ce561170a0fb74a317902ec18937377457ffce5b30932924c9dcb1321a73c3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-618d1efd836846b0cf06eb2a24c5cab7fde5952408e2d48093c334c9d12bf902</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-236032ad52b5c77d76ca8b5b9d3ee21fa9d36f49e15211204ee2de8f5df0e70a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BENCHMARK&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"BASE RATE BENCHMARK"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A reference interest rate used for calculating loan interest rates, which includes LIBOR for amounts in Dollars, EURIBOR for Euros, and CDOR for Canadian Dollars."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reference interest rates used in the loan agreement, which may undergo replacements based on market conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"“Benchmark” means the applicable Benchmark Replacement to the extent that such Benchmark Replacement has replaced such prior benchmark rate."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-30dfd32b0cc9b04004fb69c1cd353fb396870e7d97974f09ab4577578d08dfbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b591041fb8162698727d6a13b94c260ee88b2e7cbd5d43f9c27b507e795a9d60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c0f0b68eca4939163d14493fb5157bc0af66d4679ed687caf547fea769ae75c</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-236032ad52b5c77d76ca8b5b9d3ee21fa9d36f49e15211204ee2de8f5df0e70a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REVOLVING LOANS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"FACILITY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A type of loan that allows the borrower to draw, repay, and redraw loans up to a specified limit, as defined in the credit agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"A type of loan that borrowers can draw upon multiple times up to a set credit limit, as specified in the credit agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Loans that the Borrower may borrow and re-borrow prior to the Facility Termination Date as part of their credit agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Outstanding Revolving Loans will be reallocated by the Administrative Agent among the Lenders on the applicable Increased Amount Date."&lt;SEP&gt;"Revolving Loans are a type of credit facility that allows the Borrower to access funds as needed, within agreed limits under the terms of the credit agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Revolving Loans are a type of lending arrangement allowing Borrowers to draw, repay, and borrow again up to a certain limit."&lt;SEP&gt;"Revolving Loans are loans that provide the Borrower with flexible borrowing options, allowing repeated borrowings and repayments under the terms of the agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Revolving Loans refer to the credit facilities available for the Borrower, allowing for borrowing and repayment flexibility under the terms of the credit agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5c4f7a8234bc1804b6e445146a95d72695c19e55f57401948135577314a75e20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f7abefa6ccc55aca68ead2529cd1b73fe04a3bf5203cc613c26a693df88af49&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b81e8c9163be938645e4a599c88eeda4c7a60c74354129569709069236e2747&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f8d33f29a840f4d84faed83a3c1e767c065efcb42c195f8b7fa8235336825d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac2e7129863413f7a79efaf0a8f5c494d690324b6cd4ea41a5a342e206f2a1f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c89d63d96bc9f898e7d1e68ccb7e0afa2d66f4dc3885f8b3cb4e72b0a2720b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db8e590901b58e9ab12d9ef9e5f4436f0a4d1f8f01c3b35ed7eaf8a841004452&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b906346eed7e4a224403e60ffc5f35f5ff18699d55120568924463cc31dd7f3</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-236032ad52b5c77d76ca8b5b9d3ee21fa9d36f49e15211204ee2de8f5df0e70a</data>
</node>
