</node>
<node id="&quot;ERISA&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"REGULATORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Employee Retirement Income Security Act of 1974, establishing standards for pension plans in the private industry to protect plan participants."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-30dfd32b0cc9b04004fb69c1cd353fb396870e7d97974f09ab4577578d08dfbd</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-236032ad52b5c77d76ca8b5b9d3ee21fa9d36f49e15211204ee2de8f5df0e70a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;RATE MANAGEMENT TRANSACTIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"COMMITMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Financial dealings or contracts relating to the management of interest rates, mentioned as part of non-cash expenses in the calculation of Consolidated EBITDA."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rate Management Transactions include financial agreements related to interest rate risk management that affect a person's obligations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rate Management Transactions involve the financial dealings concerning hedging and management of interest rate risks that may affect the Borrower’s financial exposure."&lt;SEP&gt;"financial activities related to managing interest rates which result in gains or losses during the specified period, impacting profitability measures."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c4a351a1361d1b2bab080245c9f7cfcbfe265cb6295dad3bae410e60d8a1bc32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c3dadd9848a42e3657edcc9a12dafee9a73e1cff19c0413111e18b6834cc291&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-988baef871db4cd892d141bb544160c46b90b02279e9f9ea056c5d720e9daca3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9ee4f98e9418b2314433f25ffaac06cca4e00777385e22ab35871fe9e0364f9</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-236032ad52b5c77d76ca8b5b9d3ee21fa9d36f49e15211204ee2de8f5df0e70a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LETTERS OF CREDIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LETTER OF CREDIT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A financial instrument involved in the lending process, ensuring that payments due under the loan are guaranteed for the Borrower."&lt;SEP&gt;"A financial instrument issued by a bank guaranteeing payment on behalf of the borrower to a beneficiary."&lt;SEP&gt;"A financial instrument issued by a bank guaranteeing payment on behalf of the borrower, ensuring that borrower’s obligations will be met even if they encounter financial difficulties."&lt;SEP&gt;"A financial instrument issued by the Issuing Lender guaranteeing payment on behalf of the Borrower, as indicated in various sections of the agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"A financial instrument issued by the Issuing Lender guaranteeing payments on behalf of the Borrower."&lt;SEP&gt;"A financial instrument issued by the Issuing Lenders guaranteeing payment on behalf of the Borrower, ensuring that the Borrower's obligations will be met."&lt;SEP&gt;"Collective reference to letters of credit issued, including Existing Letters of Credit pursuant to the stated section."&lt;SEP&gt;"Financial instruments issued by Issuing Lenders guaranteeing payment on behalf of the Borrower to a beneficiary."&lt;SEP&gt;"Financial instruments issued by Lenders ensuring payment obligations are met by the Borrower, particularly during defaults."&lt;SEP&gt;"Financial instruments issued by the Issuing Lender guaranteeing payment pursuant to the agreement to ensure the Borrower's obligations are met."&lt;SEP&gt;"Financial instruments issued by the Issuing Lenders in reliance on agreements for the account of the Borrower, which facilitates additional financing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Financial instruments that ensure payment obligations are met by the borrower, providing security to the lender."&lt;SEP&gt;"Letters of Credit are financial instruments issued by a bank guaranteeing payment to a beneficiary, ensuring the borrower's obligations will be met."&lt;SEP&gt;"Letters of Credit are financial instruments issued by the Issuing Lenders guaranteeing payment on behalf of the Borrower to beneficiaries, ensuring the Borrower's obligations are met."&lt;SEP&gt;"Letters of Credit are financial instruments issued by the Lender to guarantee payment on behalf of the Borrower to a beneficiary, as outlined in the Agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Letters of Credit refers to a financial instrument issued by a bank guaranteeing payment on behalf of the borrower to a beneficiary, ensuring that the borrower's obligations will be met."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-5b23229f61676fc82b994cebe129ddba04bb9c15c7e9ebf4e7844cba0040e826&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31fbd7065e88ea9bd9a524a193a0c450e9b6d3fea3c531fb95f1ec404e0c737&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2afd79002837d6455b2622441701b97392842efbe57752aea97657f35f63be89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e62c5ad35244893d47c41c57cf2f91066b96affaf8d1e8160b7b82529c6a81d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b81e8c9163be938645e4a599c88eeda4c7a60c74354129569709069236e2747&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f8d33f29a840f4d84faed83a3c1e767c065efcb42c195f8b7fa8235336825d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9647a89a58b5dd94c4107a499b784dee152c76826fe46e047c882f3d29f4565&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72c1e23a0ce98e3ab6be8fd0ba73ff8a04834563d3bc6b6a28016942800aea96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac2e7129863413f7a79efaf0a8f5c494d690324b6cd4ea41a5a342e206f2a1f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fe353bb910c379d25fe75054e8695fd4392eba70dc8d849dcd9f86d70c5037b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-337171a55b9c980d0dcb5ffb1bd97f2bfe3343740427c244b5a793ad0cef374b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a915934b5ce2936e38d936eaf4dfcba0d99ee6b9c1b8e5e6700b27f717605157&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59684afb2e463574cf2aaf600c780e0debe3a298245661d942ad591b5ac883c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64d3d8235da6ab2d73914174a1596810ac479be1cca3c369228533b49ce78efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebe5b7adcaae8d762224c153315aceccb8e517430bcc13042391071b592f8641&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e197c6b12698708e1139425ee7f8fcca3ecd69283bc4e33a49d4d969c98e339d</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-236032ad52b5c77d76ca8b5b9d3ee21fa9d36f49e15211204ee2de8f5df0e70a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FEES, COSTS, CHARGES AND EXPENSES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"COMMITMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Normal and customary fees, costs, charges, and expenses incurred or charged by the Issuing Lender in relation to issuing or administering any Letter of Credit."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-45e5ac6c7f9fe3736f2815b71cd467c73369fe987b9b7844edefe0f26772ebbc</data>
