</node>
<node id="&quot;TERMS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CONTRACT TERM"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The stipulations and conditions defined within the Credit Agreement that govern the lending arrangement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1ce561170a0fb74a317902ec18937377457ffce5b30932924c9dcb1321a73c3a</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-236032ad52b5c77d76ca8b5b9d3ee21fa9d36f49e15211204ee2de8f5df0e70a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;FLOOR&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INTEREST RATE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Defines the minimum interest rate applicable to the debts as stipulated in the agreement, ensuring that rates do not fall below a certain threshold."&lt;SEP&gt;"the term 'Floor' pertains to the minimum acceptable rate that applies during the agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b591041fb8162698727d6a13b94c260ee88b2e7cbd5d43f9c27b507e795a9d60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d990607ca6b9c513c4d87a46d457b97a8e231369a24385de07cb159ae613ec7</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-236032ad52b5c77d76ca8b5b9d3ee21fa9d36f49e15211204ee2de8f5df0e70a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;GOODWILL IMPAIRMENT LOSSES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"COMMITMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A reduction in the value of goodwill assets, indicating a decline in the expected future profitability of the Borrower and its subsidiaries."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c4a351a1361d1b2bab080245c9f7cfcbfe265cb6295dad3bae410e60d8a1bc32</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-236032ad52b5c77d76ca8b5b9d3ee21fa9d36f49e15211204ee2de8f5df0e70a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LONDON BANKING DAY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"SCHEDULE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Any day on which transactions in Dollar deposits are conducted among banks in the London interbank eurodollar market."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b31fbd7065e88ea9bd9a524a193a0c450e9b6d3fea3c531fb95f1ec404e0c737</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-236032ad52b5c77d76ca8b5b9d3ee21fa9d36f49e15211204ee2de8f5df0e70a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;REIMBURSEMENT OBLIGATION&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"COMMITMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The Reimbursement Obligation is a specific commitment of the Borrower to repay amounts drawn under the Letter of Credit."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-afdc36e8e6e47ff0270974860558b97778e2ed65a56afbb1fb30ae1565713adc</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-236032ad52b5c77d76ca8b5b9d3ee21fa9d36f49e15211204ee2de8f5df0e70a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DISCLOSURES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"COVENANTS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Written information provided by the Borrower that is required to be accurate and not misleading, which affects the negotiation and execution of the Agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f579af8ae52777bd03c297500e3fc8f4d9da9b71f9f0ab65dbd1d3c5524bce2b</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-236032ad52b5c77d76ca8b5b9d3ee21fa9d36f49e15211204ee2de8f5df0e70a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUB-AGENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"AGENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Sub-agents appointed by the Administrative Agent perform specific duties and exercise rights under the loan documents, with operational responsibilities delegated from the Administrative Agent."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2266a9fc1a73832774525a2886a88ef57d8b9423316f0e4b0b7f4361472cabeb</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-236032ad52b5c77d76ca8b5b9d3ee21fa9d36f49e15211204ee2de8f5df0e70a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MARKO LUKIN&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"AGENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"By: /s/ Marko Lukin, Name: Marko Lukin, Title: Vice President."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b1dfcf35c71b9bc1649a0165fc3f3382c476139fd8e243735127e10bcebe9770</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-236032ad52b5c77d76ca8b5b9d3ee21fa9d36f49e15211204ee2de8f5df0e70a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;UNREALIZED LOSSES RESULTING FROM MARK-TO-MARKET ACCOUNTING&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INTEREST RATE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Reflects potential losses on financial instruments that have not yet been sold, influencing the Borrower's financial standing."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c4a351a1361d1b2bab080245c9f7cfcbfe265cb6295dad3bae410e60d8a1bc32</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-236032ad52b5c77d76ca8b5b9d3ee21fa9d36f49e15211204ee2de8f5df0e70a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;SUBSIDIARY&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"COMPANY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A Subsidiary is a company controlled by the Borrower, playing a role in the overall corporate structure and financial strategy, especially concerning the credit agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"A corporate entity affiliated with the Borrower that may benefit from the issuance of Letters of Credit, with obligations that the Borrower must support."&lt;SEP&gt;"A legal entity that is partially or wholly owned by another company (the parent company) and can act as a separate legal entity for business and operational purposes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Any entity that is a part of the Borrower's corporate structure and can also benefit from Letters of Credit issued under the agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Any entity that is controlled by the Borrower, often referred to in relation to joining the Agreement as a Guarantor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Any party that is contractually obligated to fulfill the terms of the agreement. In this context, it signifies a company controlled by the Borrower which may incur liens against its property."&lt;SEP&gt;"Describes a corporation owned or controlled by a person or its subsidiaries, usually holding more than fifty percent of the voting power."&lt;SEP&gt;"Each Subsidiary refers to any additional entities under the Borrower's control that may have specific obligations under the credit agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Subsidiaries are associated entities that the Borrower may acquire or merge with, impacting the overall financial obligations."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-ebe5b7adcaae8d762224c153315aceccb8e517430bcc13042391071b592f8641&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31fbd7065e88ea9bd9a524a193a0c450e9b6d3fea3c531fb95f1ec404e0c737&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27cc7ccadb0b52553a85f4e8ffdeee4e8a7fccc4f117304c9420bf47ea12062a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54b9f25b0f7727d8348c35e3ea577371f86853ec4e30f80fb2c8dcede9f5324a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b81e8c9163be938645e4a599c88eeda4c7a60c74354129569709069236e2747&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b77f015c45a7573c444a9980fc7601fb5db09fa6ba499d28d02463542e445a50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-933342c9998e30f355fb1fd9ac245727f7b30b12ae83c53d533846bc90d0efb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21b34c24607ec90e75db330e8f024fc166d7fb83cc0ea29a817bbe6967bcfe8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dba0097483e6d43680ca18f43e0b34befca3d229494d85657cb0d3ced4f666f</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-236032ad52b5c77d76ca8b5b9d3ee21fa9d36f49e15211204ee2de8f5df0e70a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TERMS OF LETTER OF CREDIT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"COVENANTS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Terms of Letter of Credit encompasses all conditions and stipulations that govern how the Letter of Credit operates."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-afdc36e8e6e47ff0270974860558b97778e2ed65a56afbb1fb30ae1565713adc</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-236032ad52b5c77d76ca8b5b9d3ee21fa9d36f49e15211204ee2de8f5df0e70a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;AGENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"AGENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"AGENTS refer to designated entities managing the administrative and operational aspects of the loan documents, including communication and coordination among parties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Entities or individuals appointed to represent or manage affairs on behalf of Lenders or the Borrower in connection with the Agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Agents are entities tasked with managing the administrative and operational aspects of the credit agreement, including communication and coordination among participants."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f579af8ae52777bd03c297500e3fc8f4d9da9b71f9f0ab65dbd1d3c5524bce2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8de38d9f190c7d6bcbaaaede79f19cbb59631f72bbfd31261e61e07ea73ad5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49b949bd6b938010a265fb14a53b068d725f73af78772772e2b7ee398ddb3783</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-236032ad52b5c77d76ca8b5b9d3ee21fa9d36f49e15211204ee2de8f5df0e70a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;EXCULPATORY PROVISIONS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"COVENANTS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"Exculpatory Provisions define the limits of liability for the Administrative Agent and its Related Parties against negligence or misconduct in managing duties as outlined in the Agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-2266a9fc1a73832774525a2886a88ef57d8b9423316f0e4b0b7f4361472cabeb</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-236032ad52b5c77d76ca8b5b9d3ee21fa9d36f49e15211204ee2de8f5df0e70a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;DEUTSCHE BANK AG&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"CORPORATION"</data>
  <data key="d1">"DEUTSCHE BANK AG is a global banking and financial services company involved in various financial activities including lending."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-b1dfcf35c71b9bc1649a0165fc3f3382c476139fd8e243735127e10bcebe9770</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-236032ad52b5c77d76ca8b5b9d3ee21fa9d36f49e15211204ee2de8f5df0e70a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;LOAN DOCUMENTS&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"AGREEMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">The entity "LOAN DOCUMENTS" encompasses a comprehensive set of formal and legally binding agreements that govern the terms, obligations, and rights of all parties involved in a credit arrangement. These documents outline the complete framework of the loan agreement, detailing the specific terms and conditions associated with the lending transaction, including responsibilities of the Borrower, Lenders, and any administrative agents involved.

The Loan Documents include various legal instruments such as the primary Agreement, Letter of Credit Applications, and any amendments or waivers that may arise throughout the lending process. Importantly, the Loan Documents serve to delineate the rights and obligations of the parties, forming a crucial foundation for the enforcement of contract law or tort law claims. 

The collection of these documents not only comprises the explicit terms of the loan but also details the processes for any necessary modifications through instruments like the Lender Joinder Agreements. Furthermore, they form a binding set of obligations that all parties must adhere to, ensuring that the roles and responsibilities within the credit agreement are clearly understood. Therefore, the term "Loan Documents" refers to all formal agreements, including any ancillary materials that outline the rights, responsibilities, and terms agreed upon when executing and delivering the loan, thus representing a crucial aspect of the lending landscape.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1b73fe97875c42acbd1cfd5ed3bf71a7e121ab6595dfedd5673f1192ddc8c312&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b331bb28b5b328980bc6448e64c475bba021f2fd90308da50dd38ae5cdac4acd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2cf4e13aa2c6cc0391a25d2ae2caab24fe2617aff917d82593d32932dc3f2bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b906346eed7e4a224403e60ffc5f35f5ff18699d55120568924463cc31dd7f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21b34c24607ec90e75db330e8f024fc166d7fb83cc0ea29a817bbe6967bcfe8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-998a753d13e4f1db21d4717dbf25b13a2f2c768e30ac332912250581750f06b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-758c1989597265c02f92778b7755a4eab1b74b2f2d41a5713c7b39e52d9b065c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56f8b8206fc34fa3ec46ca9b971beb5f819724a771480da0f5330492c19f3969&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b81e8c9163be938645e4a599c88eeda4c7a60c74354129569709069236e2747&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fe353bb910c379d25fe75054e8695fd4392eba70dc8d849dcd9f86d70c5037b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac2e7129863413f7a79efaf0a8f5c494d690324b6cd4ea41a5a342e206f2a1f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b591041fb8162698727d6a13b94c260ee88b2e7cbd5d43f9c27b507e795a9d60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3771cda3e13643768381b94281c30943819130272cfee9ae8ac10eee712cd1cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49b949bd6b938010a265fb14a53b068d725f73af78772772e2b7ee398ddb3783&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-030278384b922b4dde4eb789cb2a8bc568f20779afcf9493b74bd661c5c80d27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2266a9fc1a73832774525a2886a88ef57d8b9423316f0e4b0b7f4361472cabeb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b31fbd7065e88ea9bd9a524a193a0c450e9b6d3fea3c531fb95f1ec404e0c737&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c3dadd9848a42e3657edcc9a12dafee9a73e1cff19c0413111e18b6834cc291&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f8d33f29a840f4d84faed83a3c1e767c065efcb42c195f8b7fa8235336825d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c89d63d96bc9f898e7d1e68ccb7e0afa2d66f4dc3885f8b3cb4e72b0a2720b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1993053c0afe71a0a70310c159f65971f4df8e35de1ff74fef6f621fd100f0e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf023d8a063c56705dcb87212bf4c927c8978394473e8991513f7100ef2ad0e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6da2eeb855bc4db1527cd23dadabfc8740772aed447426187bdf23324a009ce5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56dfadbbf38deaf8b024ab85a1c130f8a147dc4852082a7387117676f6972937&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e290c93761fbccff21c271b66a77cdf6ae6c638e176225b143e913e3bb53382c</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-236032ad52b5c77d76ca8b5b9d3ee21fa9d36f49e15211204ee2de8f5df0e70a</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;ADMINISTRATIVE AGENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"AGENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">The Administrative Agent is a designated entity, often represented by Citibank, N.A., that plays a crucial role in managing the administrative and operational aspects of a credit agreement. This includes responsibilities such as fund disbursement, communication, and coordination among various participants, particularly lenders and the borrower. The Administrative Agent oversees administrative tasks, ensures compliance with the agreement's terms, and acts as a liaison between the lenders and the borrower.

Specifically, the Administrative Agent is responsible for managing disbursements, executing necessary documents, facilitating communication between the involved parties, and ensuring accurate record-keeping. It is authorized to manage payment processes, oversee the execution of the credit agreement, and coordinate approvals for activities such as issuing Letters of Credit. The Administrative Agent also handles the transfer of agency duties to any successor and is tasked with maintaining accounts for loans and ensuring compliance with interest rate calculations.

In addition, the Administrative Agent plays a vital role in reallocating Revolving Loans, handling obligations related to Defaulting Lenders, and managing cash collateral accounts for the benefit of lenders. It is responsible for notifying lenders about payment distributions, managing communications regarding interest calculations, and making decisions related to currency conversions in compliance with the agreement. Ultimately, the Administrative Agent is pivotal in ensuring the smooth operation and administration of the credit agreement, acting on behalf of the lenders while maintaining clear communication and function among all participants involved.</data>
