<node id="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"BORROWER"</data>
  <data key="d1">The "Borrower" is defined as the individual, company, or legal entity that receives funds under a credit agreement and is obligated to repay the loan according to the agreed terms. The roles and responsibilities relating to the Borrower encompass several key elements: 

1. **Identification**: The Borrower can include various high-level officials, such as the President, Chairman, Chief Executive Officer, Chief Financial Officer, Chief Accounting Officer, Vice Presidents, Treasurer, Assistant Treasurer, Controller, or Secretary.

2. **Obligations**: The Borrower is responsible for repaying the loan, which includes compensation for any interest and fees as stipulated in the credit agreement. Additionally, the Borrower must execute the Loan Documents and perform all obligations outlined therein.

3. **Consents and Rights**: The Borrower consents to arrangements regarding participations and agrees to maintain rights of setoff against the Administrative Agent. Furthermore, the Borrower must provide notice to the Administrative Agent for specific requests and is involved in decisions regarding administrative changes.

4. **Legal and Financial Authority**: The Borrower possesses the power and authority to execute necessary documentation, must adhere to conditions precedent, and is responsible for ensuring that it does not assign or transfer any obligations without prior written consent from the Administrative Agent and each Lender.

5. **Communication and Documentation**: The Borrower may create electronic communications and must give notice in prescribed forms concerning its financial activities, such as requests for drawings or extensions of loan maturity.

Overall, the Borrower is the entity at the center of the credit agreement, with clearly delineated responsibilities related to loan receipt, repayment, administrative dealings, and compliance with the terms specified within the loan documents.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1b73fe97875c42acbd1cfd5ed3bf71a7e121ab6595dfedd5673f1192ddc8c312&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2cf4e13aa2c6cc0391a25d2ae2caab24fe2617aff917d82593d32932dc3f2bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47592a39712b138036905fc1d1df7e9312477e32c44ad87875c7d936e87521f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-369742b947eb975088213077aacde47f5316c0bade4e9d6cf868e117dff1e43c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-656448c34d6c39d709cf4f0b3fafa8f15917e254898e468b864268232de70e76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3e41e26cebf9acc28cdb3ea223550400ffc870eb3272b969bfbe4bbb593592f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21b34c24607ec90e75db330e8f024fc166d7fb83cc0ea29a817bbe6967bcfe8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45e5ac6c7f9fe3736f2815b71cd467c73369fe987b9b7844edefe0f26772ebbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c4a351a1361d1b2bab080245c9f7cfcbfe265cb6295dad3bae410e60d8a1bc32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80a8dd5ea3f5d9c099606547630c6c1b040c3735377dece8e8b20ebc9dde7016&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-337171a55b9c980d0dcb5ffb1bd97f2bfe3343740427c244b5a793ad0cef374b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84d7361cb1344ec6b34607e1ffa71f6fa5a0707b1c2af1350dabed4ef3eb78ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-788c1a0d88f1541100bf054380b01f260c6ad5ad3928a6c14b72431c8a554338&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-933342c9998e30f355fb1fd9ac245727f7b30b12ae83c53d533846bc90d0efb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e197c6b12698708e1139425ee7f8fcca3ecd69283bc4e33a49d4d969c98e339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-030278384b922b4dde4eb789cb2a8bc568f20779afcf9493b74bd661c5c80d27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6b7cdf0d7ee80ebd481b61e63f9c51eb02289ce4b8ad902df17900f1154fafb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c3dadd9848a42e3657edcc9a12dafee9a73e1cff19c0413111e18b6834cc291&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8de38d9f190c7d6bcbaaaede79f19cbb59631f72bbfd31261e61e07ea73ad5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9508aaaa2cc35b99a72e9bfe92dfe2bfa2bab730720841a5b147639395b735ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1993053c0afe71a0a70310c159f65971f4df8e35de1ff74fef6f621fd100f0e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfae90ac75934f3a0aa495e4b1945f7c157fd6f848b6ca39885db21029c243e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a015574d7a05a08d9a207880f6e2fce97ba212fa98d485fcccecdf620633b1a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d32220edb2c51a75bea6e67cd0e5a1fbeb1a2abce31b2cffece621f54b4b8aad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff7eefa1e3ad5e4629d751cd1f37a6eef