<node id="&quot;ISSUING LENDER&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"LENDER"</data>
  <data key="d1">The "Issuing Lender" refers to a specialized financial institution that is authorized to issue letters of credit, which are financial instruments provided on behalf of the Borrower as part of a credit agreement. This entity plays a critical role in the lending process by ensuring that the Borrower meets the obligations outlined in the loan agreement. The Issuing Lender not only issues these letters of credit but is also involved in the financing arrangement, disbursing funds, and monitoring compliance with the terms of the agreement.

In this capacity, the Issuing Lender is responsible for several key functions: managing the issuance of letters of credit, ensuring payments are guaranteed to third parties, and handling the associated obligations under the credit agreement. Furthermore, the Issuing Lender may require consent for assignments related to the loan and can request cash collateralization if any defaults occur with other lenders.

Entities such as Citibank, N.A., and Crédit Agricole Corporate and Investment Bank are mentioned as Issuing Lenders, highlighting their commitment to fulfilling these responsibilities as outlined in the credit agreement. Similarly, Barclays Bank PLC is also identified as an Issuing Lender, involved in issuing various financial instruments and credits under the terms set forth in the agreement.

The Issuing Lender is entitled to reimbursement from the Borrower for any amounts paid under the letters of credit. Additionally, they may charge fees for their services. Their role also entails safeguarding against erroneous transactions and adjusting to regulatory changes that may impact their obligations. Overall, the Issuing Lender is integral to the financial transaction process between the Borrower and third-party beneficiaries, ensuring that all parties fulfill their respective commitments.</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-18226adc50d0d43fc9565aeec65a89dd9d347d5730d5e84494f8535da6419cdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b73fe97875c42acbd1cfd5ed3bf71a7e121ab6595dfedd5673f1192ddc8c312&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ca66dd52a177698fde85d2ca5aa568e9318f2e347056e6d1c7b41e4270dff9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b07eaf1cd11ad2db2417fe6ba87a7a0eb64930b9f015b722b79b572a77fc318&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e1fbadef1542fe6b85421b5736bdaa13e5a005ae9ae9a1ffea09a5d52c4d8121&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-27cc7ccadb0b52553a85f4e8ffdeee4e8a7fccc4f117304c9420bf47ea12062a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-369742b947eb975088213077aacde47f5316c0bade4e9d6cf868e117dff1e43c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fc3c63f017c57c99df34221b48c51e924cb393015709234b1ce975d2bb6bcba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b906346eed7e4a224403e60ffc5f35f5ff18699d55120568924463cc31dd7f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66fd0f9a9180e543fe5145a08d528e6028aba0d4342edd7498580d6806dc63d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45e5ac6c7f9fe3736f2815b71cd467c73369fe987b9b7844edefe0f26772ebbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-758c1989597265c02f92778b7755a4eab1b74b2f2d41a5713c7b39e52d9b065c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2e76bfe06832d96f514332019f438cc910c77413f0617abc31b13b1ced12faa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecaefa3c2ad5e19bb3010a0abd8a00b9385343a23c01dd136cc52a12bf1c8a23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b81e8c9163be938645e4a599c88eeda4c7a60c74354129569709069236e2747&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-389432f97c0d9acb329730d29e0276eba93dc70c0916c74399e531affb7eace1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b7175909aee8ce03791965ee234bfe872f940b215b4506ec0f0b1e30d0cf99d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-afdc36e8e6e47ff0270974860558b97778e2ed65a56afbb1fb30ae1565713adc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-337171a55b9c980d0dcb5ffb1bd97f2bfe3343740427c244b5a793ad0cef374b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72c1e23a0ce98e3ab6be8fd0ba73ff8a04834563d3bc6b6a28016942800aea96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7efe0d6b67c1b39367c09aa93cf17410243ba43338b16f788915ff8afce12d2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84d7361cb1344ec6b34607e1ffa71f6fa5a0707b1c2af1350dabed4ef3eb78ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a5b1ddd76b46da4f5b285127348b0ac9622761aad50db0119a29e624efdf1ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e197c6b12698708e1139425ee7f8fcca3ecd69283bc4e33a49d4d969c98e339d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80deda61594e7242d6d82b4a17cd4839b