<edge source="&quot;L/C OBLIGATIONS&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">24.0</data>
  <data key="d5">"L/C Obligations represent the effective liabilities of the Borrower related to Letters of Credit."&lt;&lt;SEP&gt;"The Borrower acknowledges L/C Obligations as part of their financial responsibilities outlined in the agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Borrower incurs L/C Obligations when letters of credit are issued on their behalf as part of the Agreement, which they are responsible for honoring."&lt;&lt;SEP&gt;"The L/C Obligations represent the amounts the Borrower must account for regarding Letters of Credit that have not yet been reimbursed."</data>
  <data key="d6">"financial obligation"&lt;&lt;"7"&lt;SEP&gt;"obligation, liability"&lt;SEP&gt;"represents, obligations"&lt;SEP&gt;"responsibility, obligation"</data>
