<edge source="&quot;ADMINISTRATIVE AGENT&quot;" target="&quot;BORROWER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">347.0</data>
  <data key="d5">The relationship between the Administrative Agent and the Borrower is structured around the management of financial transactions and compliance aspects as governed by their credit agreement. The Administrative Agent acts on behalf of the Borrower, overseeing interactions with Lenders, ensuring adherence to the terms set in the agreement, and facilitating communication related to the Borrower's obligations.

In this role, the Administrative Agent is responsible for coordinating loan transactions and managing compliance with the credit agreement. This includes notifying the Borrower about payment due dates, amounts owed under Letter of Credit arrangements, and any Benchmark Replacement changes. The Agent also maintains accounts and records of amounts owed by the Borrower to Lenders and provides written notices concerning various elements of the credit agreement.

The Borrower is obliged to communicate with the Administrative Agent regarding financial responsibilities, including payments and compliance with covenants outlined in the agreement. Any requests for funding of loans from the Borrower are managed by the Administrative Agent, provided there are no existing defaults. Furthermore, the Borrower is required to obtain the prior written consent of the Administrative Agent for certain actions, such as assignments of rights and certain payments.

Both parties engage in mutual communication, where the Borrower informs the Administrative Agent about its selection of Advances and Interest Periods and must notify the Agent about any changes related to the Loan Documents. Additionally, the Borrower provides necessary documentation and fulfills obligations, such as delivering Cash Collateral to secure its commitments.

The Administrative Agent serves an advisory role, relying on information provided by the Borrower while managing the overall relationship and compliance aspects with Lenders. The Administrative Agent also plays a vital role in documenting materials and conducting administrative actions required for the execution of the credit agreement.

Overall, the relationship is symbiotic, with the Administrative Agent relying on the Borrower to fulfill its obligations while offering guidance and managing the administrative and operational functions critical to the Borrower's loan transactions.</data>
