<edge source="&quot;BORROWER&quot;" target="&quot;LENDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">288.0</data>
  <data key="d5">The relationship between the Borrower and the Lender is established through a contractual agreement, wherein the Borrower receives financial support from the Lender under the specified terms of the credit agreement. The Borrower is legally bound to repay the funds provided by the Lender, which includes both the outstanding principal and any associated fees, as per the agreed-upon payment schedule.

The Borrower's obligations encompass making timely payments as stipulated in the loan documents, ensuring compliance with the terms of the agreement. Additionally, the Borrower may invite the Lender to offer further financing, such as an Incremental Revolving Credit Commitment, and may require the Lender to assign its rights and obligations under certain conditions, provided that prior written consent is obtained.

The Lender, in turn, is responsible for disbursing the funds and monitoring the Borrower's adherence to the terms laid out in the credit agreement. This relationship is characterized by mutual obligations, with the Borrower expected to honor their financial commitment to repay the loan while the Lender facilitates the necessary funding.

In summary, the Borrower holds a significant financial obligation to repay the amount received from the Lender under the terms outlined in the credit agreement, with both parties having defined roles in this lending arrangement.</data>
